WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.560
The Expanse Season 5 finale is out now, and&nbsp;
we made a video explaining the mysteries and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.200
character arcs of the season – which you can&nbsp;
watch at the link below if you haven’t already.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.160
But there’s also a lot of cool stuff in the&nbsp;
book series that wasn’t included in Season 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.120
Like Bobbie surfing a missile in space and&nbsp;
saving the Martian prime minister – for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.240
example. As well as lots of character&nbsp;
moments, world details, and thematic stuff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.440
So how does Season 5 of the show compare to the&nbsp;
books, and what cool bits didn’t get included?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.640
This video has info from the first five books&nbsp;
and the novellas, but no spoilers from the later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.240
books, so it’s safe if you just watch the show.
Each book in The Expanse is told from the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.200
of view of a different set of characters. So&nbsp;
the first five books all have Holden chapters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.720
but Book 1 also has Miller chapters,&nbsp;
Book 2 has Avasarala and Bobbie and Prax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:59.040
Book 3 has Anna Clarissa and Bull,&nbsp;
Book 4 Elvi Basia and Havelock. Book 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.960
Nemesis Games, is the first time we get chapters&nbsp;
from Naomi, Amos and Alex’ point of view.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.000
In the early books, Amos and Alex are pretty minor&nbsp;
characters – they’re actually more fleshed out in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.080
the TV show. But in Book 5, each of the Roci crew&nbsp;
go off on their own stories, and we get inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:22.400
their heads for the first time, as the worlds&nbsp;
change dramatically around them. Season 5 adds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:29.760
plotlines about Avasarala and Drummer, but Nemesis&nbsp;
Games is about Holden, Alex, Naomi and Amos.&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:37.120
So when Holden is alone on Tycho, he really&nbsp;
struggles to cope. He needs to be around people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.560
but he’s uncomfortable with how strangers treat&nbsp;
him like a celebrity. So Holden spends some nights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.880
in a crappy Italian restaurant drinking mediocre&nbsp;
margaritas, and before long, he is crying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:55.440
drunk on bourbon with his pants off, talking to&nbsp;
his spaceship in in the dark. Being unable to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.640
his crew when they’re in danger is a nightmare for&nbsp;
Holden, and his emotions are all over the place.&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.560
Luckily, Monica keeps him busy. In the TV&nbsp;
show, Monica investigates a plot to steal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.920
Fred’s protomolecule. But in the book, Monica&nbsp;
investigates colony ships that have disappeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:17.440
at the Ring gates. In the show, there’s just one&nbsp;
ship that disappears in the finale, destroyed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:24.320
mysterious aliens. But in the book, there’s a&nbsp;
dozen civilian ships that just disappear. At&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.520
first, Monica and Holden think this is related&nbsp;
to Marco and Duarte’s black market ships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.560
and it’s only at the end of the book that they&nbsp;
realise, oh shit, aliens have been eating people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:40.480
this whole time, those colony ships were destroyed&nbsp;
by the entities in the Ring. At one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:46.160
Monica asks Holden to use Fred’s protomolecule to&nbsp;
try to reconnect to the consciousness of Miller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.920
and ask him what’s vanishing the ships, like a&nbsp;
séance to summon a ghost – but Holden refuses.&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.520
So Monica gets kidnapped, and in the books,&nbsp;
it’s kind of Holden’s fault. Cause Holden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.560
blabs about Monica’s investigation to&nbsp;
Sakai, who is secretly working for Marco.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:09.280
So once again, Holden’s habit of sharing sensitive&nbsp;
information creates trouble. As Avasarala says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:14.640
Holden’s “record for blurting information”&nbsp;
“is the stuff of legend”. But later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.320
Holden chooses to keep it secret that Fred’s&nbsp;
protomolecule was stolen, to prevent panic –he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:26.480
actually withholds information for once. So Holden&nbsp;
does learn from his mistakes, he’s “changed”.&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.480
Holden and Fred find Monica because Monica’s&nbsp;
terminal is still connected to her hidden camera.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.960
In the books, there’s an extra step here&nbsp;
because Monica’s terminal is smashed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.320
The device still works, but the screen is&nbsp;
shattered and scrambled into shards of glass.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:49.600
So they get help from a scientist. Astronomers&nbsp;
interpret light that reflects and refracts around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:55.360
planets and stars and stuff. So the scientist uses&nbsp;
those same principles to decipher the light that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:02.720
scattered by this smashed screen, creating like a&nbsp;
digital lens to resolve it into a visible image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:08.080
and that’s how they find Monica. So it’s always&nbsp;
cool when there’s some science in the sci fi.&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:15.360
In the show, Marco’s people attack Tycho and&nbsp;
kill Fred Johnson. In the book, Fred does get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:22.240
shot, but he survives. In fact, he fights back&nbsp;
this attack in badass fashion. He toughs out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.360
the bullet-wounds, coordinates a defence, and&nbsp;
he uses this secret code he’s got with Drummer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:33.440
to set an ambush on the attackers. After all,&nbsp;
this is “Colonel Frederick Lucius Johnson”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:39.680
“the Butcher of Anderson Station”, “traitor to&nbsp;
Earth”, he’s an experienced military tactician,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.520
he’s prepared for this kind of thing, so he&nbsp;
fights back and survives. Still, Marco’s attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:55.600
and the rise of the Free Navy is a huge blow to&nbsp;
Fred politically. He no longer speaks for the Belt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.520
when these radicals are in power. Anderson Dawes&nbsp;
tells Fred that he’s gotta cooperate with Marco,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.960
and Fred seriously considers joining&nbsp;
Marco’s side, and trying to make peace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:13.840
moderating the radicals from within. Holden says&nbsp;
it’s be bullshit for Fred to change sides again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:19.280
like when he left Earth to help the Belt.&nbsp;
But Fred says he “never changed sides”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:26.080
“The sides keep changing around” him. Fred will&nbsp;
join whatever faction can do the most good, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:33.280
in this new political situation, it’s not obvious&nbsp;
which faction that is. Holden argues that Marco is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:39.120
obviously the bad guy here, and ultimately Fred&nbsp;
goes to work with Avasarala, Earth and Mars.&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.320
Alex goes back to Mars to reconnect&nbsp;
with his ex-wife Talissa. In the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:50.720
they have a son called Melas, but in the books&nbsp;
Alex doesn’t have a son – as far as he knows.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:57.440
Avasarala once mentions that Alex has a&nbsp;
son he doesn’t know about, which is weird.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:03.360
Did Talissa hide his son from him? Or is the&nbsp;
mother some other woman? The books don’t say.&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:09.040
Alex helps Bobbie investigate black market&nbsp;
Martian military gear – so in the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:14.240
Alex talks with Sauveterre and Babbage.&nbsp;
But in the books, Alex talks to Duarte.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:21.200
Duarte appears to be just this average military&nbsp;
bureaucrat guy, described as likeable, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:27.280
competent. Duarte tells Alex that’s he’s aware of&nbsp;
the black market ships and is investigating, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:33.200
is powerless to stop it. It’s only at the end of&nbsp;
the book that you realise ‘holy shit, that Duarte&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:39.200
guy was lying, he was the secret mastermind behind&nbsp;
the black market ships and Laconia all along.&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.000
So Alex and Bobbie investigate missing ships on&nbsp;
the Razorback, and in the book they also rescue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:52.240
the Prime Minster of Mars, from an attack by&nbsp;
Marco – Marco’s plan is even more ambitious in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:58.160
the books, trying to kill the leader of Mars&nbsp;
as well as Fred Johnson and Holden and Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:05.040
The Martian Prime Minister’s name is Nathan Smith,&nbsp;
he’s described as “polite” and “Inoffensive” and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:11.200
he just sort of tags along in the back seat while&nbsp;
Alex and Bobbie go save Naomi. But when Bobbie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:17.040
wears her power armour, she can’t fit in her seat&nbsp;
on the Razorback, so she rips out the seat and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:22.560
just stands there whole time, bracing herself&nbsp;
on the walls in high g with sheer strength.&nbsp;

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.320
The Razorback can’t safely get to Naomi&nbsp;
fast enough, so Bobbie hops on missile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:33.360
and rides it as it’s fired next to Naomi,&nbsp;
and that’s how they grab her in the book.&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:39.520
But in the show, they race in on the Razorback,&nbsp;
and Alex dies of a stroke from their high g burn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:45.680
which is a risk they mention in the books. But&nbsp;
in Book 5, Alex doesn’t die – it looks like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:49.360
they killed him off in the show because&nbsp;
the actor isn’t returning next season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:56.480
Maybe in the show, Bull will take his place as&nbsp;
pilot on the Roci. Bull is a weird addition to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:02.160
show, cause in the books, he only appears in Book&nbsp;
3, playing a similar role to Drummer in Season 3.&nbsp;

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:09.200
Naomi is taken prisoner by her emotionally&nbsp;
manipulative terrorist ex Marco and their son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:16.480
Filip. And in the book she goes to a really dark&nbsp;
place – all the old trauma and fear and guilt from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:23.200
her past comes flooding back. Being around Marco&nbsp;
again makes her question her identity – is she a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:29.440
prisoner, a terrorist collaborator, a mother&nbsp;
– she doesn’t know which is “her real self”.&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.880
In her despair, Naomi draws strength by thinking&nbsp;
of Amos. She asks herself “What would Amos do?”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:42.960
Which is funny, because Amos is not exactly&nbsp;
a great model of wisdom and decision-making.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:50.400
But Amos’ resilience and emotional detachment&nbsp;
is what Naomi needs to survive this fear and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:56.160
trauma. And at the same time that Naomi draws&nbsp;
strength from Amos, Amos thinks of Naomi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:01.040
and tries to emulate her, in his relationship&nbsp;
with Clarissa. So it’s beautiful that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:06.800
even when they’re a zillion miles apart, Naomi&nbsp;
and Amos’ bond makes both of them stronger.&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:14.000
So Marco attacks Earth, kills billions of people,&nbsp;
and starts a militant Belter uprising, and in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:20.480
book, he has more specific reasons for doing&nbsp;
this. Cause Belters are a people and a culture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:26.480
adapted to space, their economy is based on mining&nbsp;
asteroids in the Belt. But now there are hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:32.240
of new worlds beyond the Ring with resources that&nbsp;
are way easier to extract, on planets with free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:40.160
air and water. So the asteroids and stations of&nbsp;
the Belt have no economic future. But Belters’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:47.040
bodies are adapted to life in low gravity – in the&nbsp;
books, Belters look different to inners, they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:53.680
tall and thin, with big heads and weak bones.&nbsp;
Many Belters can’t survive on a planet with full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:59.600
gravity, like how Naomi couldn’t live on Ilus.&nbsp;
And for the Belters who can live on planets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:06.240
after a generation in gravity, they wouldn’t be&nbsp;
Belters anymore. The Ring is a threat to the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:12.560
existence of the Belter people, so part of Marco’s&nbsp;
goal is to block off access to the Ring gate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:18.960
He lets Duarte go to Laconia, but doesn’t let&nbsp;
anyone else through, holding the solar system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:25.520
captive to preserve a future for the Belt.
Fred compares Marco to Alexander the Great,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:31.920
who defeated a Persian emperor at the Battle of&nbsp;
Gaugamela – which is the title of Episode 4. At&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.200
Gaugamela, Alexander was way outnumbered,&nbsp;
but he won because he “saw an opportunity”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:43.920
and was brave and audacious enough to take it –&nbsp;
just like Marco had the audacity to defeat Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:51.520
But Fred wonders if Marco really is as Great as&nbsp;
Alexander, or if he just thinks he is. The book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:59.600
emphasises how fake and superficial Marco is. He’s&nbsp;
really good at appearing noble and powerful, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:06.560
it’s a “mask”. And when that mask slips,&nbsp;
Naomi sees a “rage-filled boy” behind it.&nbsp;

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:14.000
When Naomi and Holden reunite, at the end of the&nbsp;
book, Naomi tells Holden about Marco and Filip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.880
and her past for the first time. When she leaves&nbsp;
at the start of the book, she doesn’t tell Holden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:24.160
where she’s going, just that she needs to go&nbsp;
do something, and needs to do it herself. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:29.920
important to her that Holden respects Naomi’s&nbsp;
right to fight her own battles, and keep her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:37.280
secrets. Holden has to learn that doesn’t get to&nbsp;
know everything or control everything. Naomi tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:42.800
Holden about her past when she’s ready, on her own&nbsp;
terms, and that makes their bond even stronger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:49.280
After recovering from her ordeal, Naomi&nbsp;
feels at peace for the first time in a while.&nbsp;

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:56.080
Amos goes back to Earth, and on the way, he meets&nbsp;
a Belter couple called Jianguo and Rico. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:01.440
book, these guys have a daughter called Wendy,&nbsp;
and Amos makes a special effort to protect her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:08.080
and buys her an ice cream. He later sees a street&nbsp;
kid in Baltimore, and wants to help him too. Amos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:14.080
has always had a particular need to help children,&nbsp;
because of how terrible his own childhood was.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:18.480
Amos’ backstory is explored&nbsp;
in a novella called The Churn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:24.240
and the show included the basic details&nbsp;
– as a child, Amos’ name was Timothy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:31.280
and he was sexually exploited in organised crime.&nbsp;
A woman called Lydia was like a mother to Timothy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:37.280
What the show leaves out is that in The Churn,&nbsp;
when Timothy was about fifteen, he and Lydia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:43.920
also had a sexual relationship. It says they&nbsp;
weren’t lovers, they weren’t mother and son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:49.680
they were just Lydia and Timothy, and in&nbsp;
their strange complicated relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:56.560
they found comfort in each other. In the show,&nbsp;
Amos picks up this glazed mug – which is mentioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:02.560
in The Churn as a gift that eight-year-old&nbsp;
Timothy gave Lydia for her birthday. So Timothy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:11.520
and Lydia’s relationship was tender and wrong&nbsp;
and sweet and dark and it made Amos who is now.&nbsp;

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:19.840
After the asteroids hit, the books describe the&nbsp;
apocalyptic devastation of Earth. Ash rains down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:25.760
coating everything with a layer of gray, blocking&nbsp;
out the sun like “A funeral shroud” “over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:32.960
planet”. All the plants start dying, animals freak&nbsp;
out. All over the world, food and water runs out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:38.880
there’s riots and looting. “The birthplace&nbsp;
of humanity” is “in its death throes”, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:46.320
billions die. Unlike the other characters, Amos&nbsp;
doesn’t feel horror or fear at this catastrophe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:53.360
He doesn’t worry about what he can’t control. He&nbsp;
only thinks about how to survive in the present.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:58.880
So Amos and Clarissa escape the Pit, and&nbsp;
survive apocalyptic America together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:05.760
Amos calls Clarissa “Peaches” because in Book 3,&nbsp;
Clarissa called herself Melba, and a Peach Melba&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:12.160
is a kind of dessert, so Peaches. He also calls&nbsp;
Clarissa “little tomato” once, for some reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:18.880
which is adorable. Previously, Amos called&nbsp;
Anna “Red”, cause she’s a redhead in the books.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:24.480
Amos calls Konecheck “Tiny”, which is interesting&nbsp;
because in The Churn, Amos’ crime boss called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:31.440
Amos “Tiny”. So Amos is a man with a fake&nbsp;
name, who calls others by many different names.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:36.640
There’s a moment in the show where Clarissa&nbsp;
mentions faking an ID, and Amos and Erich smile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:42.640
at each other. Because in The Churn, Erich created&nbsp;
the fake ID that made Timothy into Amos Burton.&nbsp;

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:49.200
So Amos and Clarissa and Erich find a ship to&nbsp;
escape Earth at Lake Winnipesaukee. It’s an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:54.640
enclave where rich people have holiday homes, and&nbsp;
the books describe how luxurious everything is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.640 --> 00:15:02.000
with mansions, and boathouses, and a genetically&nbsp;
engineered dog, and this ship the Zhang Guo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:08.640
The books describe its opulent decorations in&nbsp;
silver and gold and velvet and it’s this giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:14.640
lavish, totally impractical ship – more a&nbsp;
statement of wealth than a means of transport.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:21.040
Avasarala later calls it a “gaudy turd”.&nbsp;
And this highlights the inequality on Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:26.720
We’ve seen that many people live in poverty and&nbsp;
squalor on Basic. And here are these “Assholes”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:33.280
with mansions bigger than housing blocks that&nbsp;
would fit thousands. But in the end, that wealth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:38.720
doesn’t mean shit in the apocalypse – it’s the&nbsp;
mansions’ staff, along with Amos and Clarissa and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:44.400
Erich, who use the ship to escape Earth.
Amos says that in times of conflict,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:49.920
human groups fracture into small hostile&nbsp;
tribes. Everything that keeps society&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:56.080
civilised like laws and countries and money are&nbsp;
just stories, and when the shit hits the fan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.080 --> 00:16:03.200
those stories die, and violence starts. Clarissa&nbsp;
has a more optimistic inclusive perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:08.400
like when she makes friends with the staff at&nbsp;
Winnipesaukee to peacefully grow their tribe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:15.520
So she tells Amos that yes, peace and civilisation&nbsp;
are just stories, but people are good at telling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:21.440
stories that can bring people back together.
In the end, Amos brings Clarissa to join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:26.560
the crew on the Roci – even though Clarissa&nbsp;
tried to kill them all once. And in the book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:32.560
he physically smuggles her onto the ship&nbsp;
inside a crate, and she pops out like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:39.600
jack-in-a-box and scares Alex and it’s great.
So overall, Season 5 is a pretty close adaptation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:44.880
of Nemesis Games, though reading the book&nbsp;
does add detail and depth. Throughout all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:50.560
the storylines in Book 5, there’s a lot of&nbsp;
thought and reflection about aging and change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:56.400
In Nemesis Games, the worlds and politics&nbsp;
of The Expanse are dramatically shaken,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.400 --> 00:17:03.040
heading for a radically different future. But the&nbsp;
characters are still so defined by their pasts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:11.920
“Shit changes and doesn’t”, Erich says. Naomi&nbsp;
thinks Things change, and they don’t change back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:18.080
We can’t undo the damage of the past.&nbsp;
But even when everything goes wrong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:25.280
and our tribes are split apart, we’re really good&nbsp;
at telling stories to put things back together.&nbsp;

